      "role": "user",
      "content": "Professor, I'm working through some signal processing problems and I'm stuck on the intuition behind noise. If I have a signal contaminated with random noise, how does the Fourier Transform actually allow us to distinguish between the \"true\" signal and the \"noise\" part? Mathematically, why does the noise end up spread across the spectrum while the signal stays concentrated in specific frequency bins?",
